    "field": "Physical oceanography",
    "problem": "Accurately quantifying the Indonesian Throughflow's impact on global climate is challenging due to the region's complex geography, intense mixing, and temporal variability, which existing sparse and non-simultaneous measurements have failed to fully capture.",
    "method": "This paper describes the International Nusantara Stratification and Transport (INSTANT) program, which uses simultaneous mooring deployments in key inflow and outflow passages to measure the full-depth velocity, temperature, and salinity profiles of the Indonesian Throughflow over a multi-year period to quantify its magnitude and variability.",
    "task": "The paper's task is to describe the complex physical oceanography of the Indonesian seas to understand and quantify the Indonesian Throughflow (ITF), detailing its pathways, water mass transformations, and significant impacts on regional and global ocean circulation and climate.",
