            "relation": "OBSERVED_IN_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Australia",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "The eastern Indian Ocean is also affected by the ITF. Here, the buoyancy introduced to the eastern tropical Indian Ocean by the ITF sets up a southward pressure gradient that results in a southward flow of warm surface water along the west coast of Australia, called the Leeuwin Current (Smith et al., 1991).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
